      en: "The Monastery of Santes Creus in Catalonia is a prime example of Cistercian architecture. Founded in 1150, its church combines Romanesque and Gothic styles. It houses the tombs of kings Peter III and James II of Aragon. The 14th-century Gothic cloister is renowned for its intricate carvings. The monastery was a spiritual and political center. After the 19th-century confiscation, it fell into disrepair but was restored in the 20th. Now it is a museum and national monument.",
